    pr_ref:  # c358
    description: "PRE-REGISTERED. The method below is fixed BEFORE the data is looked at, deliberately.\nThe owner's ruling is \"I adjudicate, owner spot-checks\", which puts the labelling in the\nhands of the party with an interest in the answer; writing the rubric after seeing the\nflows is how that quietly becomes self-marking. Nothing here may be revised once\nadjudication starts without recording the revision and the reason on this item.\n\nWHY IT CANNOT RUN YET, verified 2026-08-10 rather than assumed. The only adjudicable\nfinding population on hypergumbo's own tree is the 1,890 flows on its two violated\nself-claims (runtime-cli-no-host-fs 1,148; runtime-cli-no-subprocess 742). Those are\nexplicitly PARKED on the WI-vanun thread with a recorded trigger: revisit when WI-votom\nis done AND INV-lupav L2/L3 are closed, or when INV-busis receives its 7a/7b ruling.\nChecked: WI-votom done; INV-busis unruled; INV-lupav L2 closes through WI-joluk's\ncoverage gate, which IS BUILT but wired only to the BARRIER arm -- the section 3a arm is\nunwired deliberately, because wiring alone is a no-op and must land in the same PR as the\nremoval authority. So L2 is NOT closed and the trigger has NOT fired. (Correction: the\nWI-vanun thread's own wording says WI-joluk is \"todo_hard and unstarted\". That is stale\n-- the gate exists. The conclusion is unchanged, for the correct reason.)\n\nTHE ONLY PRIOR DATAPOINT, and why it is weak. WI-ruhol closed 2026-03-25 at 50%\nprecision (3 of 6) against its own decision gate (\">80% = Phase 2 lower priority; <50% =\nhigh priority\") -- landing exactly ON the boundary, on a SYNTHETIC reference impl, before\nany of the nine phases shipped. It cannot be compared to a post-phase number, and\nre-running it on fixtures would reproduce its weakness rather than answer the question.\n\nSAMPLE FRAME. Stratify the 1,890 by the two axes that are already known to partition\nbehaviour, then sample WITHIN strata rather than uniformly, because a uniform sample of a\npopulation where one claim holds 61% would mostly measure that claim:\n  A. claim (host_fs 1,148 / subprocess 742)\n  B. analysis_method (`precise`/ddg vs `approximate`/structural) -- INV-sadah's axis, and\n     the one where a labelling error is a DIFFERENT defect rather than a precision miss\nTarget n = 60, allocated proportionally within stratum, minimum 10 per cell. 60 gives a\n+/-13pp 95% interval on a 50% rate -- coarse, and stated so nobody quotes it to the point.\n\nADJUDICATION RUBRIC, fixed in advance. For each sampled flow, label exactly one:\n  TRUE POSITIVE   source genuinely reaches sink with no sanitizer, READ AGAINST SOURCE.\n                  The bar is a reader following the path in the file, not the tool's own\n                  path field agreeing with itself.\n  FALSE POSITIVE  any link in the chain does not exist in the source.\n  UNADJUDICABLE   the path cannot be followed from source alone (dynamic dispatch,\n                  reflection, a hop through a language with no extractor). This is a\n                  THIRD label, not a coin-flip into one of the first two, and its share\n                  is reported -- WI-tizig already records that 16.4% of pooled evidence\n                  rows sit outside any walked function and can never be adjudicated by\n                  section 3a. Precision is reported over TP/(TP+FP) with the\n                  UNADJUDICABLE count printed beside it, never folded in.\n\nADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION. Every label gets a second pass by an agent that did NOT produce\nit, given the flow and the source but NOT my label, and charged with reaching its own\nverdict; a third agent adjudicates disagreements. Fresh agents, never forks of my\ncontext, per the standing panel rule. Disagreement RATE is published as a headline number\nalongside precision -- a 3% disagreement rate and a 30% one mean very different things\nabout a 60%-precision claim, and hiding it would make the estimate look sharper than it is.\n\nOWNER SPOT-CHECK PACKAGE. Hand over: (1) the full stratified sample as a table -- flow id,\nclaim, analysis_method, source symbol, sink symbol, hop count, my label, verifier label,\nfinal label; (2) the 10 flows where the two passes disagreed, in full; (3) the source\nexcerpts for a random 10 of the TRUE POSITIVES, so the owner can check the labels I was\nmost confident about rather than only the contested ones; (4) this rubric, unedited.\n\nWHAT WOULD CHANGE WHAT. >80% precision: section 7a/7b stay parked and the removal\nauthority (WI-kabif) becomes arguable on its merits. 50-80%: report and do nothing --\nthat is the band WI-ruhol already sat in and it moved no decision. <50%: precision is the\nheadline problem and recall work should stop until it is understood. State the band the\nresult lands in BEFORE computing the interval, so the interval is not used to move it.\n\nKNOWN BIAS I CANNOT CONTROL, stated rather than managed away: I wrote much of the code\nbeing measured this month. The adversarial pass and the owner spot-check are the only\nmitigations, and neither is blinding."  # c358
    fields: {}  # c358
