  nonce: 5d4b  # 5d4b
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-08-25, measurement 0005 (P3 of the taint-root campaign): RUN THE BLIND SECOND PASS. Asked explicitly because this session forbids subagents unless the owner asks, and because 0004 could NOT reproduce this items pre-registered adversarial verification and named that as its weakest part. 0005 gates the owners P6 re-rank, so it gets the strong method: primary pass by me, then fresh agents (never forks) given the flow and the source but NOT my label, a third agent on disagreement, and the DISAGREEMENT RATE published as a headline number beside precision -- exactly as this item pre-registered. The alternatives offered and declined were (a) 0004s single-pass with ties-to-FP and (b) single-pass now with a blind pass only if the result lands near the 50% band edge."  # 5d4b
- op: discuss  # e07c
  at: '2026-08-25T20:11:46Z'  # e07c
  by: agent  # e07c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e07c
  clock: 5  # e07c
  nonce: e07c  # e07c
  message: "THE PRE-REGISTERED METHOD ON THIS ITEM WAS EXECUTED IN FULL for measurement 0005, and this is the record of it.\n\nWhat this item fixed in advance and what actually happened:\n- RUBRIC: 0001's, verbatim, including the control-dependence-only convention and the in-program-computation tie-break. Given to every adjudicator in the same words; the text is in the run directory as blind/RUBRIC.md.\n- ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION (\"every label gets a second pass by an agent that did NOT produce it, given the flow and the source but NOT my label\"): RUN. Four independent adjudicators over disjoint chunks covering all 37 situations, each forbidden from reading any ledger, any prior measurement, or the ledger-building scripts.\n- DISAGREEMENT RATE PUBLISHED AS A HEADLINE (this item's requirement): 0/37 = 0.0%. That includes both contested cases -- caddy's stdin-config-to-autosave chain, which the second pass reconstructed hop for hop including a hop I had inferred rather than read, and cmdRespond, where the second pass independently found the shadowed `var false bool` that disables the autosave guard.\n- A THIRD AGENT ON DISAGREEMENT: not needed for the blind pass, there were none. Two FURTHER passes were commissioned anyway, precisely because this item's own caveat says a zero is not evidence of correctness, and BOTH of them moved the headline: (1) an adjudication of the one contested label OVERTURNED THE PRIMARY PASS -- caddy's config-field sinks are TP, not UNADJUDICABLE, because the rubric makes reflection an instance of unfollowability and the path is followable from in-repo declarations (row rate 7.9% -> 10.6%); (2) an adversarial refuter BROKE 1 OF THE 9 TRUE POSITIVES -- Fernet.decrypt authenticates before decrypting, so a wrong CI_BUILD_KEY raises InvalidToken rather than changing the written bytes, which makes the key a gate rather than a contributor (situation 24.3% -> 21.6%, row 10.6% -> 10.0%). FINAL: 21.6% per situation, 10.0% per row.\n- BLINDNESS CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSERTED: the 37 packets are generated mechanically and were consumed by both passes; grepping them for verdict vocabulary returns nothing, none names a ledger or a prior measurement, the rubric names no specific flow, and the chunk manifests were asserted to be a partition before the pass ran.\n\n0001's OWN CAVEAT IS REPRODUCED IN THE WRITE-UP AND SHOULD BE READ WITH THE ZERO: a low disagreement rate shows the RUBRIC is applied consistently; it is NOT evidence the rubric is right, because both passes share it. Those two further checks are the evidence FOR that caveat rather than a formality: the blind pass alone would have published a number that was wrong in both directions at once.\n\nONE ERROR IN MY OWN INSTRUCTIONS, disclosed by the agent that hit it. The four blind chunks were explicitly forbidden the ledger-building scripts; the refuter's prompt named only ledger-*.json and docs/measurements/. It grepped the run directory while checking what the packets' `collapsed pairs` field counts, landed in make_pair_ledger.py (which embeds primary rationales for six of the nine), stopped immediately, and stated that all nine of its verdicts predate that read. It matters less than it would for a blind pass -- the refuter was TOLD the nine TP labels in its own prompt, so what leaked is rationale rather than verdict -- but it is recorded in the measurement rather than quietly fixed.\n\nThe decision bands on this item are NOT touched. They were named before any interval was computed and only the owner applies them."  # e07c
- op: discuss  # bcc3
  at: '2026-08-31T00:47:39Z'  # bcc3
  by: agent  # bcc3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bcc3
  clock: 6  # bcc3
  nonce: bcc3  # bcc3
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-08-30 — THE BAND IS RETIRED AS AN AUTOMATIC GATE AND REPLACED\nBY A MECHANISM TEST.\n\nTHE RULING, in the owner's terms:\n  1. ACCURACY WORK IS ALWAYS IN.\n  2. NEW-SURFACE WORK CARRIES ITS OWN PRECISION ESTIMATE.\n  3. THE NUMERIC THRESHOLD IS RETIRED AS AN AUTOMATIC GATE.\n\nWHAT THIS REPLACES. This item pre-registered \"<50% => precision is the headline\nproblem and recall work should stop until it is understood\", and measurement\n0006 tripped the ADR-0046 restatement of it at 24.1% useful precision. That\nstop has gated the campaign since. It is now lifted, not by the number moving,\nbut because the rule was shown to rest on a premise the evidence does not\nsupport.\n\nTHE PREMISE THAT FAILED: that recall work and precision work TRADE OFF. Three\nindependent measurements say they mostly do not.\n  - The dominant FP family is 0006's family A, \"primitive classified by NAME,\n    not by what it does\" -- its own words, \"the single most consequential\n    family\". Fixing it IS catalogue work, the same activity as recall work, and\n    it deletes false findings AT THE SOURCE rather than suppressing real ones.\n  - Every suppression lever is measured and empty or backwards. Filtering to\n    `ddg` gives 100% precision, keeps 7 of 85 flows and LOSES 21 OF 28 TRUE\n    POSITIVES (0001/0005). Section 7a's removal authority has ZERO addressable\n    domain -- 0 of 153 rows (0007). The cross-function composition ceiling pays\n    backwards: refutation bounded at zero, confirmation INFLATES output by up\n    to 778 rows on a cohort emitting 298 (0008).\nSo stopping recall work bought no precision. It stopped work.\n\nTHE DISTINCTION THE BAND DID NOT MAKE, and which the new rule does: work that\nmakes an EXISTING row more accurate improves precision (it is precision work\nwearing a recall label), while work that adds NEW SURFACE is genuinely dilutive\nat ~26% useful precision -- roughly three false for every true. WI-lipis is the\ncase that makes it concrete: ~19% of its measured population is pure\nfalse-source deletion and the rest adds true sources, so a blanket stop blocked\na net-precision-positive change.\n\nWHY THE THRESHOLD IS RETIRED RATHER THAN RE-SET. The band is no longer\nresolvable by the instrument that feeds it. Useful precision projects to 26.7%\n(27 useful of 101) against a 25% line -- a 1.7-point gap, where the 95%\ninterval at n=101 is roughly 18.1%-35.4%. Putting 26.7% on one side of 25%\nwould need about 2,600 adjudicated situations, ~23x the budget this frame calls\n\"the only real cost knob\". The band was sound when the number was 41%, where a\n+/-8-point interval still discriminates; at 24-27% it does not. A decision rule\nthat has drifted into the region where its own instrument cannot resolve it\nshould say so on its face rather than wait to be rediscovered.\n\nWHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. That precision is \"understood\" is a judgement, not a fact:\nthe mechanisms are named and counted, but nobody has shown that fixing all of\nthem lands above any particular number. And none of the evidence above measures\nRECALL -- every figure in the series is precision-only, so \"the tool misses\nthings\" remains unquantified. The paired study authorised in the same exchange\nmeasures DIRECTION of travel, not level, and is scoped to say so."  # bcc3
- op: discuss  # 8968
  at: '2026-08-31T01:23:45Z'  # 8968
  by: agent  # 8968
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8968
  clock: 7  # 8968
  nonce: '8968'  # 8968
  message: "PAIRED PRECISION STUDY — RESULT (owner-authorised 2026-08-30). Direction of\ntravel only; this design cannot resolve an absolute level and is scoped to say\nso. Analyzer SHA 8e8ca2f285 recorded per ADR-0048 A1, which 0006 could not do.\n\nMETHOD. Re-collect 0006's 16-repo cohort on the current tree (22 min, 675\nsituations), pair against 0006's 112 adjudicated situations by identity, carry\nthe labels of situations that did not change, and blind-adjudicate only those\nwhose chain moved. Two independent passes per repo, fresh agents, given the\nflow and the source but not the prior label, walled off from every ledger.\n\n                            0006          now\n  population                 112           97\n  true positives              38           29\n  correctness precision     33.9%        29.9%\n  vacuous still live          11            6\n  useful precision          24.1%        23.7%\n\n  disagreement rate: 0 of 7 (0.0%)\n  lost from population: 15 (6 TP / 9 FP)\n\nDIRECTION: FLAT on useful precision, DOWN on correctness. Nothing here supports\n\"precision is improving\". The haskell db_* deletion removed 5 vacuous findings\nas intended; the 6 bash /dev/null deductions NEVER LEFT (INV-kosur: the discard\ngate is wired to the io-boundary claim path and not the taint-flow path); and\nthree rabbitmq true positives were refuted by the blind panel.\n\nTWO METHOD ERRORS OF MY OWN, caught by controls and recorded with the result\nrather than quietly fixed:\n 1. The first identity key embedded LINE NUMBERS in source_symbol, so 0006's\n    own family-E span defect (one C file uniformly shifted by 4 at both ends)\n    reported tmux#1 as lost when server_destroy_pane is still present at\n    309-383. Re-keyed on (claim, file, symbol name, sink).\n 2. An apparent LOST TRUE POSITIVE (gocryptfs#2) is not lost: its source is\n    test.bash, and the run discloses `excluded_flows: {\"test_sourced\": 2}` --\n    WI-bifob excluding test-sourced flows by default and disclosing rather than\n    dropping them. Correct behaviour. Filing it as a regression was one step\n    away and only reading the verdict's own excluded_flows field prevented it.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT SUPPORT. An absolute level: at n=97 the 95% interval is\nroughly +/-8 points, which is why the owner retired the numeric threshold as an\nautomatic gate in the same exchange. Recall: nothing here measures it. And the\nunchanged 90 situations carry 0006's labels rather than fresh ones, which is\nwhat makes this a PAIRED design and not a re-measurement."  # 8968
